# Salesforce Summer Training – Day 12

## 1. What is Salesforce DX?

Salesforce DX (Developer Experience) is a modern development approach that enables:

* Source-driven development
* Version control integration
* Better team collaboration
* Faster deployments

### Key Benefits

* Work with code instead of only using the UI
* Track changes using Git
* Easy deployment across environments
* Supports modular development

---

## 2. Why CLI Matters

Salesforce CLI allows developers to interact with Salesforce using the terminal.

### Advantages

* Faster than manual clicks
* Automates repetitive tasks
* Enables scripting and automation
* Improves developer productivity

### Example Uses

* Deploy code
* Run tests
* Create orgs
* Retrieve metadata

---

## 3. Why GitHub Matters

GitHub is used for version control and collaboration.

### Benefits

* Tracks code changes
* Enables team collaboration
* Supports branching and merging
* Provides backup and history

### Developer Workflow Thinking

#### Why Use GitHub + CLI + DX Instead of the Browser?

Browser-based development has several limitations:

* Slow and manual process
* No proper version tracking
* Difficult to collaborate
* Higher risk of overwriting changes

### Modern Tools Enable

* Automation
* Collaboration
* Scalability
* Reliability

---

## 4. Team Collaboration Problems (Without Tools)

If multiple developers work on the same project without a proper workflow, several issues can occur:

* Code conflicts
* Overwriting changes
* No version history
* Difficult debugging
* No rollback capability
* Deployment errors

### Enterprise vs College Coding

| College Assignments   | Enterprise Development           |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Small projects        | Large-scale systems              |
| Single developer      | Multiple developers              |
| Minimal testing       | Extensive testing                |
| Simple deployment     | Structured deployment            |
| Low complexity        | High complexity                  |
| Limited collaboration | Team collaboration               |
| Basic maintenance     | Rollback and recovery mechanisms |

---

## 5. Enterprise Workflow Discussion

Enterprise systems require:

### Version Control (GitHub)

* Tracks changes
* Maintains project history
* Supports collaboration

### Branching Strategy

* Enables parallel development
* Prevents conflicts in production code

### Testing

* Ensures reliability
* Detects issues before deployment

### Deployment Pipeline

* Supports safe and controlled releases
* Reduces deployment risks

### Rollback Mechanism

* Allows recovery from failures
* Minimizes downtime and business impact

